t/id #uuid "aec0cd94-20e4-5748-b9c1-4de7b1854a8e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Problems Involving Multiplying Negative Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "5f3cfae7-b7d6-56b2-a245-6ec44b76e462" :question/math-academy-id "e-22714" :question/problem "The temperature of a liquid decreases by $\\dfrac{4}{5}\\,^\\circ\\text{C}$ each minute for $\\dfrac{3}{2}$ minutes. What is the total change in temperature?" :question/worked-solution "The temperature decreases by $\\dfrac{4}{5}\\,^\\circ\\text{C}$ each minute.\n\nSince the temperature decreases, the change each minute is $-\\dfrac{4}{5}.$\n\nThe change occurs for $\\dfrac{3}{2}$ minutes, so the total change is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{2} \\times \\left(-\\dfrac{4}{5}\\right).\n$$\n\nEvaluating the product, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{2} \\times \\left(-\\dfrac{4}{5}\\right)\n= -\\dfrac{3 \\times 4}{2 \\times 5}\n= -\\dfrac{12}{10}\n= -\\dfrac{6}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total change in temperature is $-\\dfrac{6}{5}\\,^\\circ\\text{C}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502129 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502066 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b6c3c0b-b541-5b1f-810b-d9c4ffa1fe9c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Problems Involving Dividing Negative Numbers"}] :question/id #uuid "9c400da4-eba5-58aa-8ee5-a33269adfa2a" :question/math-academy-id "e-22728" :question/problem "Over the course of $6$ hours, the temperature of a liquid decreases by $9.6^\\circ\\text{C}$ in total. Assuming the temperature decreases at a constant rate, what is the change in temperature each hour?" :question/worked-solution "Since the temperature decreases by $9.6^\\circ\\text{C}$ over $6$ hours, the total change is $-9.6^\\circ\\text{C}.$\n\nThis change occurs evenly over $6$ hours, so we divide the total change by $6{:}$\n\n$$\n-9.6 \\div 6\n$$\n\nEvaluating the quotient, we get\n\n$$\n-9.6 \\div 6 = -1.6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the temperature changes by $-1.6^\\circ\\text{C}$ each hour."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502120 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502069 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f589fffd-f5c4-590e-9ed1-01c20390700f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Problems Involving Multiplying Negative Fractions and Mixed Numbers"}] :question/id #uuid "7be163d0-2103-5467-9bba-a4090855cc8b" :question/math-academy-id "e-22729" :question/problem "A submarine descends $1\\,\\dfrac{3}{8}\\,\\text{m}$ each minute from sea level. What is the submarine's elevation after $\\dfrac{8}{3}$ minutes?" :question/worked-solution "The submarine descends $1\\,\\dfrac{3}{8}\\,\\text{m}$ each minute.\n\nSince the elevation decreases, the change each minute is $-1\\,\\dfrac{3}{8}.$\n\nThe descent lasts $\\dfrac{8}{3}$ minutes, so the total change in elevation is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{8}{3} \\times \\left(-1\\,\\dfrac{3}{8}\\right).\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the mixed number as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n-1\\,\\dfrac{3}{8} = -\\dfrac{1\\times8 + 3}{8} = -\\dfrac{11}{8}\n$$\n\nSo the expression becomes\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{8}{3} \\times \\left(-\\dfrac{11}{8}\\right).\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the product:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{8}{3} \\times \\left(-\\dfrac{11}{8}\\right)\n= -\\dfrac{8 \\times 11}{3 \\times 8}\n= -\\dfrac{11}{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the submarine's elevation after $\\dfrac{8}{3}$ minutes is $-\\dfrac{11}{3}\\,\\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092028 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092188 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc5fba78-066d-56fb-b5ac-6733fa0349bd" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying and Dividing Negative Numbers"}] :question/id #uuid "0c43effb-b65a-503b-b56a-aac7d499ba0a" :question/math-academy-id "e-4867" :question/problem "The average temperature in Helsinki, Finland, in January $2017$ was $-5.5^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}$. If the average temperature (measured in degrees Celsius) in Yakutsk, Russia, in the same month was eight times lower, what was the average temperature in Yakutsk in January $2017$?" :question/worked-solution "To determine the temperature in Yakutsk, we multiply the temperature in Helsinki by $8$. This gives\n\n$$\n(-5.5^{\\circ}\\, \\textrm{C}) \\times 8 = -44^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average temperature in Yakutsk in January $2017$ was $-44^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092032 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092192 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "623e299c-b14a-5fba-aa7e-3fe556be7c6e" :knowledge-point/title "Combining Operations on Negative Numbers"}] :question/id #uuid "2111bc1e-b9e1-58b1-873f-d8f94b8446ff" :question/math-academy-id "e-5100" :question/problem "Martin has an overdraft facility authorized by his bank. His bank balance at the beginning of the month was $-\\[math] 550$.\n\nTo reduce his debt with the bank, Martin deposited some money into his account. After making the deposit, his new balance was $\\dfrac{2}{5}$ of the initial balance. Then, at the end of the month, Martin made a withdrawal of $\\[/math] 40$.\n\nWhat was Martin's bank balance at the end of the month?" :question/worked-solution "To determine Martin's bank balance after he made the deposit, we multiply the initial balance by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n(-\\[math] 550) \\cdot \\dfrac{2}{5} =-\\[/math] 220\n$$\n\nMartin's bank balance was updated again when he made a withdrawal. To determine the final balance, we subtract the amount of money he withdrew from $-\\[math]220$. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\[/math] 220 - \\[math] 40 =-\\[/math] 260\n$$\n\nTherefore, Martin's bank balance at the end of the month was $-\\[math] 260$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092150 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092303 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "413e7e81-2cd5-5954-835e-aa1da05e7dc5" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Negative Fractions and Mixed Numbers"}] :question/id #uuid "ed21898f-dfc1-543a-bf57-313c6e94dd63" :question/math-academy-id "e-9770" :question/problem "The temperature in a chamber that holds chlorine is $-24\\dfrac{1}{3}{^\\circ}\\textrm{F}$. It's known that chlorine boils at $\\dfrac{6}{5}$ the chamber's temperature measured in degrees Fahrenheit. What is the boiling temperature of chlorine?" :question/worked-solution "To find out the boiling temperature of chlorine, we need to calculate\n\n$$\n-24\\dfrac{1}{3} \\times \\dfrac{6}{5}\n$$\n\nFirst, we write\n\n$$\n-24\\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$\n\nas an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n-24\\dfrac{1}{3} = -\\dfrac{24\\times 3 + 1}{3} = -\\dfrac{73}{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(-\\frac{73}{3}) \\cdot \\frac{6}{5} &= -\\frac{73 \\cdot 6}{3 \\cdot 5} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{73 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3}{3 \\cdot 5} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{73 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3}{3 \\cdot 5} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{73 \\cdot 2}{\\cdot 5} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{146}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{146}{5} = -29\\dfrac15\n$$\n\nTherefore, chlorine boils at\n\n$$\n-29\\dfrac15{^\\circ}\\textrm{F}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502152 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502068 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aec0cd94-20e4-5748-b9c1-4de7b1854a8e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Problems Involving Multiplying Negative Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8297df33-3945-557a-8b12-47cba0ef0ebe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501715} {:answer/id #uuid "cf62465d-ee5a-56f9-9205-cdbc67e9ed15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501877} {:answer/id #uuid "e3b02612-0eeb-5065-9a7a-a11e62b8557c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501924} {:answer/id #uuid "e9c706d3-0dd0-5ebe-87cc-56a68f59d32f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{3}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501938} {:answer/id #uuid "f0c9430f-5d3d-51ad-9d23-0d3aa66de7ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501948}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0c9430f-5d3d-51ad-9d23-0d3aa66de7ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501948} :answer-field/id #uuid "2536844b-ad4a-5ed6-bce8-3971a2720b4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501989}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d71152b6-16b1-5e4e-a992-55dfd11f6205" :question/math-academy-id "q-357085" :question/problem "The temperature of a liquid decreases by $\\frac{3}{4}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each minute for $\\frac{8}{3}$ minutes. What is the total change in temperature?" :question/worked-solution "The temperature decreases by $\\frac{3}{4}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each minute.\n\nSince the temperature decreases, the change each minute is $-\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\nThe change occurs for $\\frac{8}{3}$ minutes, so the total change is\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{3}\\times (-\\frac{3}{4}).\n$$\n\nEvaluating the product, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{3}\\times (-\\frac{3}{4})=-\\frac{8\\times 3}{3\\times 4}=-\\frac{8}{4}=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total change in temperature is $-2{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502136 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502067 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d7b67c1-aa22-5106-9f09-19e361dc25c0" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Problems Involving Multiplying Negative Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "323f42d9-16a4-5acf-9cc5-8859e990fe96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6.5{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501557} {:answer/id #uuid "3eeb4fae-9881-59af-88ed-061e86ee17f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501579} {:answer/id #uuid "b492ba8a-773f-5ff9-8fc4-080ff2e1ee05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12.5{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501827} {:answer/id #uuid "b6e6aa31-02dc-578b-9a36-596c23908306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.5{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501830} {:answer/id #uuid "ed396f58-48ed-5ba7-a6e4-ffec135a596a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed396f58-48ed-5ba7-a6e4-ffec135a596a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501942} :answer-field/id #uuid "c409ab7a-8f68-58a9-b465-46b591b77113" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b43654ae-4e3f-5d53-a4fb-91c5e392ca63" :question/math-academy-id "q-357178" :question/problem "The temperature inside a freezer drops by $2.5{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ every hour for $4$ hours. What is the total change in temperature after $4$ hours?" :question/worked-solution "The temperature decreases by $2.5{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each hour.\n\nSince the change is a decrease and occurs for $4$ hours, the total change can be written as repeated subtraction of $2.5:$\n\n$$\n{{-\\,2.5-2.5-2.5-2.5}_{⏟}}_{4\\text{ times}}\n$$\n\nRepeated subtraction can also be written using multiplication:\n\n$$\n4\\times (-2.5)\n$$\n\nEvaluating the product, we get\n\n$$\n4\\times (-2.5)=-10.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total change in temperature after $4$ hours is $-10{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502107 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502067 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d7b67c1-aa22-5106-9f09-19e361dc25c0" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Problems Involving Multiplying Negative Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a594372-b35f-56e0-8a4d-c8bc0a7cac29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501601} {:answer/id #uuid "540050c3-f925-5073-ba35-875e0a5410ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.2{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501620} {:answer/id #uuid "8dbd0a5d-1b3f-5e92-8b30-75467294492e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6.2{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501740} {:answer/id #uuid "9930447e-e336-59d4-8781-ef16c146a7ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501755} {:answer/id #uuid "bd16380a-95d8-5088-91a0-1e14c23a1ed1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4.8{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501845}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a594372-b35f-56e0-8a4d-c8bc0a7cac29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501601} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae5ea86b-1b58-58c4-94fc-072bc0079348" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502037}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "62ed462d-094a-533c-8c38-e7a5c2d0177d" :question/math-academy-id "q-357179" :question/problem "The temperature in a city decreases by $1.2{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each hour for $5$ hours. What is the total change in temperature after $5$ hours?" :question/worked-solution "The temperature decreases by $1.2{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each hour.\n\nSince the change is a decrease and occurs for $5$ hours, the total change can be written as repeated subtraction of $1.2:$\n\n$$\n{{-\\,1.2-1.2-1.2-1.2-1.2}_{⏟}}_{5\\text{ times}}\n$$\n\nRepeated subtraction can also be written using multiplication:\n\n$$\n5\\times (-1.2)\n$$\n\nEvaluating the product, we get\n\n$$\n5\\times (-1.2)=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total change in temperature after $5$ hours is $-6{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502068 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aec0cd94-20e4-5748-b9c1-4de7b1854a8e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Problems Involving Multiplying Negative Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "035b5582-aa17-529b-b101-df7971bd9920" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{76}{21}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501471} {:answer/id #uuid "0792a188-0269-58cf-97bd-516b8fe89cfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501485} {:answer/id #uuid "2881adf2-dc78-54da-838f-2275d55fed05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501539} {:answer/id #uuid "57cf6cec-0ed9-5d2e-af3f-5ae7420f7f35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{76}{21}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501630} {:answer/id #uuid "ca9bde92-27d8-57f7-b7da-25ad1a8a9ba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{20}{7}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501870}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0792a188-0269-58cf-97bd-516b8fe89cfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501485} :answer-field/id #uuid "7180b989-67d5-5e43-9459-6d581302e067" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502015}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8734cff-4115-50f2-9d56-00580f475192" :question/math-academy-id "q-357194" :question/problem "A hot air balloon descends $\\frac{7}{3}\\,\\text{m}$ each second. What is the total change in altitude after $\\frac{9}{7}$ seconds?" :question/worked-solution "The hot air balloon descends $\\frac{7}{3}\\,\\text{m}$ each second.\n\nSince the altitude decreases, the change each second is $-\\frac{7}{3}.$\n\nThe descent lasts $\\frac{9}{7}$ seconds, so the total change in altitude is\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{7}\\times (-\\frac{7}{3}).\n$$\n\nEvaluating the product, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{7}\\times (-\\frac{7}{3})=-\\frac{9\\times 7}{7\\times 3}=-\\frac{9}{3}=-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total change in altitude is $-3\\,\\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502155 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502066 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b6c3c0b-b541-5b1f-810b-d9c4ffa1fe9c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Problems Involving Dividing Negative Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0526a325-4b35-5b86-a878-5e5333d9b326" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-27.5\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501477} {:answer/id #uuid "468f4a53-73ca-5783-986e-b0ce29a8bef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6.5\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501594} {:answer/id #uuid "806ff764-e2bf-53ab-a9cc-959d31c2dd1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.5\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501710} {:answer/id #uuid "88f6a9ce-4009-53d8-bdfd-4c51b0d6115e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.5\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501729} {:answer/id #uuid "bcf3493c-5645-5e25-b1b7-3b5b96d5ae7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5.5\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "468f4a53-73ca-5783-986e-b0ce29a8bef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6.5\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501594} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7059ce5-8fc3-5070-9a81-481986539eb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502062}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e034c9b1-b463-56a2-afff-761ad637fb35" :question/math-academy-id "q-357210" :question/problem "A diver descends a total of $32.5\\,\\text{m}$ over $5$ minutes at a constant rate. What is the change in elevation each minute?" :question/worked-solution "Since the diver's elevation decreases by $32.5\\,\\text{m}$ over $5$ minutes, the total change is $-32.5\\,\\text{m}.$\n\nThis change occurs evenly over $5$ minutes, so we divide the total change by $5:$\n\n$$\n-32.5÷5\n$$\n\nEvaluating the quotient, we get\n\n$$\n-32.5÷5=-6.5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the change in elevation each minute is $-6.5\\,\\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502066 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b6c3c0b-b541-5b1f-810b-d9c4ffa1fe9c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Problems Involving Dividing Negative Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3caccba4-e28b-5060-9476-d0d56ad94536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-$1.50$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501574} {:answer/id #uuid "7d8506be-22ad-55b5-bbe0-f44209833338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-$3.45$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501701} {:answer/id #uuid "833f4adb-8fe6-510b-969d-25198280fdef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-$2.85$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501717} {:answer/id #uuid "acdceadf-9079-5ff6-89bd-6306c8f35b37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-$4.90$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501810} {:answer/id #uuid "bccc070b-f1a6-5003-8b9e-144f4fd5600b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-$2.45$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bccc070b-f1a6-5003-8b9e-144f4fd5600b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-$2.45$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501843} :answer-field/id #uuid "e39eeddb-5bfa-5977-9c82-e89755970e04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502053}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf763c67-fa75-5f72-8661-230a30b13c07" :question/math-academy-id "q-357219" :question/problem "Over $6$ days, $$14.70$ is deducted from a transit card balance due to daily fares of equal size. What is the change in the balance each day?" :question/worked-solution "Since the balance decreases by $$14.70$ over $6$ days, the total change is $-$14.70.$\n\nThis change occurs evenly over $6$ days, so we divide the total change by $6:$\n\n$$\n-14.70÷6\n$$\n\nEvaluating the quotient, we get\n\n$$\n-14.70÷6=-2.45.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the change in the balance each day is $-$2.45.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502119 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502069 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f589fffd-f5c4-590e-9ed1-01c20390700f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Problems Involving Multiplying Negative Fractions and Mixed Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2268a62f-af3b-5554-9392-93550ebd3f67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501524} {:answer/id #uuid "34f958da-773f-515f-abd1-d2b6edb53bc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501563} {:answer/id #uuid "8075dcdc-4e30-5eab-9850-ab4d6e913258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{14}{3}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501711} {:answer/id #uuid "a46483a5-c5e1-536a-a0d5-b280e918e22b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501784} {:answer/id #uuid "ab74afde-81f9-5e89-9f65-02cca1c6532c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{4}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501806}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a46483a5-c5e1-536a-a0d5-b280e918e22b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501784} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae216ed6-c5e7-5d88-9e19-dcdfe886b809" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7b837a54-b40c-5dbd-9c93-92d2c8b04271" :question/math-academy-id "q-357241" :question/problem "The temperature of a chemical solution decreases by $\\frac{4}{5}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each minute for $3\\,\\frac{3}{4}$ minutes. What is the total change in temperature?" :question/worked-solution "The temperature decreases by $\\frac{4}{5}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each minute.\n\nSince the temperature decreases, the change each minute is $-\\frac{4}{5}.$\n\nThe change occurs for $3\\,\\frac{3}{4}$ minutes, so the total change is\n\n$$\n3\\,\\frac{3}{4}\\times (-\\frac{4}{5}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the mixed number as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n3\\,\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{3\\times 4+3}{4}=\\frac{15}{4}\n$$\n\nSo the expression becomes\n\n$$\n\\frac{15}{4}\\times (-\\frac{4}{5}).\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the product:\n\n$$\n\\frac{15}{4}\\times (-\\frac{4}{5})=-\\frac{15\\times 4}{4\\times 5}=-\\frac{60}{20}=-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total change in temperature is $-3{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502092 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502069 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f589fffd-f5c4-590e-9ed1-01c20390700f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Problems Involving Multiplying Negative Fractions and Mixed Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05436460-8fd0-5eaf-8d02-d2f20514c78b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501478} {:answer/id #uuid "134d188d-b9c3-552f-b921-1183370fb0c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501501} {:answer/id #uuid "21a0e148-8730-5869-a663-8249c3f4a7ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501523} {:answer/id #uuid "a9b9e3db-75fc-500b-be46-121b7aace8d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501799} {:answer/id #uuid "bbaec04f-5284-5518-89e1-55d6d0d563f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9b9e3db-75fc-500b-be46-121b7aace8d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501799} :answer-field/id #uuid "14daa8e3-e1bb-5707-81d3-5bbf9b88123d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "361640a2-f197-5749-a9e6-5d3176000185" :question/math-academy-id "q-357243" :question/problem "The temperature inside a freezer decreases by $\\frac{3}{5}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each minute for $1\\,\\frac{1}{4}$ minutes. What is the total change in temperature?" :question/worked-solution "The temperature decreases by $\\frac{3}{5}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each minute.\n\nSince the temperature decreases, the change each minute is $-\\frac{3}{5}.$\n\nThe change occurs for $1\\,\\frac{1}{4}$ minutes, so the total change is\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\times (-\\frac{3}{5}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the mixed number as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1\\times 4+1}{4}=\\frac{5}{4}\n$$\n\nSo the expression becomes\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{4}\\times (-\\frac{3}{5}).\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the product:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{4}\\times (-\\frac{3}{5})=-\\frac{5\\times 3}{4\\times 5}=-\\frac{15}{20}=-\\frac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total change in temperature is $-\\frac{3}{4}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}.$"}]}
